    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d945">

                <pb facs="0743" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/1579.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>To the Department it appears that either the first or third plan of confirming
                    the presidency of Diaz would accord with Martinez’s note of November 5, 1910, to
                    Dawson, and also the Assembly’s decree of December 31, 1910, electing Diaz Vice
                    President. Make suitable expression of this Government’s satisfaction with the
                    Diaz Government’s assurance of its desire to continue with the program.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
